cable <BR>  <BR>  <BR>  <BR>Here is what I could get from PI Emery Goad´s notes on the videoscrene: XXXXX= blacked out &#40;the name of the possible BTK suspect&#41;,   <BR>sn= Skov´s note <BR>  <BR>XXXXX <BR>XX <BR>  <BR>She told me in about 1986, she lived near 13th and Garland she &#62;sn :her is missing about 3-6 words,&#60; <BR>Wicki W &#40;SP&#41; murder, wich occured across the street from &#62;sn:her is missing about 4-8 words&#60; <BR>on west 13th, about 1986 <BR>  <BR>Crossman told me the following information <BR>  <BR>  <BR>1 She and her sister both dated, at about this time, a guy known as &#34;TK&#34; <BR>  <BR>2 She said her husband used to live with XXXXX <BR>  <BR>3 She said XXXX told her and her sister that he killed Vicki W and he was BTK <BR>  <BR>4 She said he molested W children after he had met W at church <BR>  <BR>5 She said XXXX told her he also knew policeofficer Landwehr from church XXXX and Landwehr were friends and this is why Landwehr would never arrest <BR>  <BR>6 She to me in about 1986, she lived near !#th and Garland she <BR>Wici W &#40;SP&#41; murder, wich occured across the street from  <BR>on west !#th, about 1986 <BR>Crossman told me the following information <BR>  <BR>Garland St.Wichita,ks: <BR><a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=U7xcK.p_0To.lgk4CeQVrC75cw--&amp;csz=Wichita%2BKS&amp;country=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=U7xcK.p_0To.l gk4CeQVrC75cw--&amp;csz=Wichita&#43;KS&amp;country=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf =0</a> <BR>  <BR>Vicki Wergeler was murdered and lived here: <BR><a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?zoomin=yes&amp;name=&amp;ed=auIIY.p_0TqHbJgwho3ioLD6nyljTH.4lQETZ63YsytcN1LYlwo.DlrvhL.V3cy36DkkfCdzf3dZwNBX3JgCwtPDLTS.SjNOCAh0q5BFnvaojGk-&amp;state=KS&amp;csz=Wichita%2C%2BKS%2B67203-1929&amp;ds=n&amp;uzip=67203&amp;mag=2&amp;desc=&amp;country=US&amp;dma=678&amp;cat=&amp;resize=l&amp;trf=0&amp;rezoom=0&amp;.intl=us&amp;compass=&amp;pan_x=0&amp;pan_y=0&amp;panable=1" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?zoomin=yes&amp;name= &amp;ed=auIIY.p_0TqHbJgwho3ioLD6nyljTH.4lQETZ63YsytcN1 LYlwo.DlrvhL.V3cy36DkkfCdzf3dZwNBX3JgCwtPDLTS.SjNO CAh0q5BFnvaojGk-&amp;state=KS&amp;csz=Wichita%2C&#43;KS&#43;67203- 1929&amp;ds=n&amp;uzip=67203&amp;mag=2&amp;desc=&amp;country=US&amp;dma=67 8&amp;cat=&amp;resize=l&amp;trf=0&amp;rezoom=0&amp;.intl=us&amp;compass=&amp;p an_x=0&amp;pan_y=0&amp;panable=1</a> <BR>  <BR><a href="http://www.cybersleuths.com/cgi-bin/ultimatebb.cgi?ubb=get_topic&amp;f=2&amp;t=000950" target=_top>http://www.cybersleuths.com/cgi-bin/ultimatebb.cgi ?ubb=get_topic&amp;f=2&amp;t=000950</a> <BR>Christen Iman noticed that the BTK on the Toasties Box looks like &#34;13 TK&#34;: <BR>So has this som credability? is BTK´s real name initials TK? like in the PI´s notes? <BR>  <BR>Here are what I could find of info on the PI Emery Goad and BTK : <BR>  <BR>Newsreport April 1, 2004 <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:DySnAV5CHMcJ:www.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite%3Fpagename%3DKWCH%252FMGArticle%252FWCH_BasicArticle%26c%3DMGArticle%26cid%3D1031774649720%26path%3D%2B%22Emery%2BGoad%2B%22%2B%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:DySnAV5CHMcJ:ww w.kwch.com/servlet/Satellite%3Fpagename%3DKWCH%252 FMGArticle%252FWCH_BasicArticle%26c%3DMGArticle%26 cid%3D1031774649720%26path%3D&#43;%22Emery&#43;Goad&#43;%22&#43;%2 Bbtk&amp;hl=en</a> <BR>  <BR>newsreport feb 1987: <BR><a href="http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:tyH6Fcg0mdgJ:www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/history/10297015.htm%2B%22bTK%22%2B%2B%2B%22emery%2Bgoad%22&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:tyH6Fcg0mdgJ: www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/bt k/history/10297015.htm&#43;%22bTK%22&#43;&#43;%2B%22emery&#43;goad %22&amp;hl=en</a> <BR>  <BR>  <BR>  <BR>The Chuch angle: <BR>This is the  churches Vicki was connected to: <BR>St. Andrew&#39;s Lutheran Church Pastor: Arno Meyer <BR> map : <a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=albzLep_0TrMZBU1FjMnOSMl4wDsZMxyeQ--&amp;csz=WICHITA%2BKS%2B67204&amp;country=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=albzLep_0TrMZ BU1FjMnOSMl4wDsZMxyeQ--&amp;csz=WICHITA&#43;KS&#43;67204&amp;count ry=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0</a>  <BR>Bill Wergelr said feb 1987: Religion is helping to ease the pain, Wegerle said. After years of shying away from church services, Wegerle has become a Sunday regular at St. Andrew&#39;s <BR>&#34;She was quite involved in babysitting, especially for church events,&#34; said the Rev. Arno Meyer, pastor of St. Andrew&#39;s. <BR>sn: so does it have som significanze that Bill Vickies husband apparently did NOT attend church while Vicki obviously had a VERY strong connection to the church&#40;es&#41;? <BR>Wegerle volunteered her time as a babysitter both at St. Andrew&#39;s Lutheran Church, which she regularly attended, and at the Asbury United Methodist Church, which was in her neighborhood. <BR>  <BR>Asbury United Methodist Church, which was in her neighborhood.  <BR>assistant pastor :Robert Winslow <BR>Map: <a href="http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=74YnTOp_0Tohhdz1eR7m0LI04VtKIIWRAQ--&amp;csz=WICHITA%2BKS%2B67203&amp;country=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0" target=_top>http://maps.yahoo.com/maps_result?ed=74YnTOp_0Tohh dz1eR7m0LI04VtKIIWRAQ--&amp;csz=WICHITA&#43;KS&#43;67203&amp;count ry=us&amp;cat=&amp;trf=0</a> <BR>today Robert Winslow workes here, also pic of RW:<a href="http://www.gbgm-umc.org/haysvilleumc/" target=_top>http://www.gbgm-umc.org/haysvilleumc/</a> <BR>  <BR>Intersting and strange statment from a Wergelre neighbor: <BR>Another neighbor echoed the woman&#39;s thoughts: &#34;I don&#39;t think anyone here is hitting the panic button,&#34; he said. &#34;They&#39;re not alarmists around here. It could happen anywhere; it could happen to your house tonight.&#34; <BR>  <BR>Well foks, I guess we just have to go research as good as we can to see if we can find somthing on this. <BR>  <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
